input, (ii) nonlinear dynamics, (iii) macroscopic limit, NONE of which hold. The empirical wavelet α=0.85 is a smoothness signature of the sum-of-cosines structure; α=0.27 after moving-avg detrending is an artifact (residual is oscillation-dominated, fit r²<0.85). **Cramér model control** D_C with independent Bernoulli(1/log n) shows the same FFT peak pattern in same bins (random-walk artifact at sampling resolution) and similar smooth raw α≈0.95 — the chi_P / Cramér distinction lies in the deterministic-arithmetic vs stochastic origin, NOT in any KPZ-class roughness signature. **Closure mode E** (structural reduction): KPZ universality is structurally inapplicable to PNT-error-term roughness. Adds **edge E2.27** (11th orthogonal pseudorandomness category, regularity-structures / Tracy-Widom). NOT a circumvention of E3.1 / E7.18 — orthogonal scale and observable. **CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §3** Hairer regularity structures / KPZ universality / Tracy-Widom β=2 promoted PROPOSED → USED PARTIAL with mode E and edge E2.27 reference. **Cites** E3.1 GUE pair correlation, C5 Stein method (S108), C7/E7.18 FHK (S133), S74 free cumulants, E2.13–E2.26 (13 prior orthogonal pseudorandomness categories). Cross-domain refs: Hairer 2014 *Inventiones* 198, 269 = arXiv:1303.5113; Tracy-Widom 1994 *Comm. Math. Phys.* 159, 151; Corwin 2012 = arXiv:1106.1596. See `experiments/analytic/kpz_pi_li_d43/`. | 157 |
